wrote:
> Hi all.
> 
> Are sayings, proverbs and the like acceptable in Lojban? Taking
> the piss out of someone, kicking the bucket or sweating like a pig
> aren't exactly logically correct phrases.

malglico -- descriptor for things that have been poorly imported
from Lojban to English, as well as stupid English tricks in general

mrobi'o ne'i lo ganxo -- "dies in the arse".  Said of something you
would like to go away.  lu mrobi'o ne'i lo ganxo li'u cu la'a
malglico

do mo -- "What's up?"

I'm sure there are others, but I'm drawing a blank right now.

